    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier start with a dominant 83.29 efficiency score. The combination of a favorable matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez (4.89 xERA) and an elite environment boost (+16% park factor) makes him the clear anchor of the lineup. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) presents a high-upside play against Kyle Gibson, benefiting significantly from a +19% SP skill advantage and +16% park boost. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.20) faces a tougher arm in Luis Castillo, his dynamic platoon edge (+14%) and spot in the two-hole keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier, serving as a vital engine for our run production today.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel**, who finished just outside the starting cut at 47.45. While he remains a steady asset, the optimizer prioritized the high-ceiling efficiency of **Andy Pages** (62.03) and **Kyle Tucker** (67.23) against a vulnerable Burke, S, whose 4.14 xERA provides a clear path for production. **Brayan Rocchio** was an easy exclusion today; facing the elite Tarik Skubal (2.82 xERA), his score plummeted to 36.43, failing to cross our established 40-point floor. \n\nInvestors should monitor the final lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Dominic Smith**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Andy Pages**, and **Josh Jung**, as all remain \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled them under the assumption of their expected spots, any defensive adjustments or surprise rest days for **Kyle Tucker** or **Josh Jung** could necessitate a pivot to **Nolan Schanuel** or **Wade Meckler** to ensure we aren't burning game caps on bench production. With **Nasim Nunez** struggling against the high-velocity, high-hold threat of Luis Castillo, we are leaning heavily on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** to carry the day\u2019s offensive output.",
